uld have** marks the desirable action that the context says did not happen.","B":"Must have would claim a strong deduction that it happened, contradicting the context.","C":"Will have would express a different prediction or inference, not the requested retrospective advice.","D":"Can have does not make the normal retrospective-advice pattern."}}},{"id":"3118ae35-1dec-555a-a685-38b16344742e","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"You did the task, but it was unnecessary: “You ____ have restored the old portrait.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"should"},{"id":"B","text":"need not"},{"id":"C","text":"must not"},{"id":"D","text":"did not need"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The action **happened**, and the speaker says there was **no need** for it.","explanation":"**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary.","keywords":["unnecessary-completed-action"],"skill":"unnecessary-completed-action","contextKey":"past-modals-2","fingerprint":"ca5e9a90f111cb7c068625b681ad296b0778c7ab4027d9e829c875042c8134c4","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The action **happened**, and the speaker says there was **no need** for it.","**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary.","Choose **need not**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Should have would recommend the action, not say it was unnecessary.","B":"**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary.","C":"Must not have does not express the stated lack of necessity in this construction.","D":"Did not need requires to before have and is not the needn’t-have pattern."}}},{"id":"83305808-84b1-55f6-acfe-73b6ba0c4962","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"Infer an ongoing past activity: “At that time, they might have ____ the old portrait.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"been restoring"},{"id":"B","text":"being restoring"},{"id":"C","text":"be restoring"},{"id":"D","text":"restoring"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Combine past possibility with continuous aspect: **might have been + -ing**.","explanation":"After might have, use **been restoring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time.","keywords":["past-continuous-deduction"],"skill":"past-continuous-deduction","contextKey":"past-modals-2","fingerprint":"e1868cb9c596bc886229b85aeea38fb1892817e36eb8a0c1d497b7734875344f","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Combine past possibility with continuous aspect: **might have been + -ing**.","After might have, use **been restoring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time.","Choose **been restoring**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After might have, use **been restoring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time.","B":"Have requires the participle been, not being.","C":"Base be cannot follow perfect have.","D":"Been is missing between have and the -ing form."}}},{"id":"55953995-f2f0-535d-a165-3ab097ea8a50","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"Make a past deduction: “She must ____ the garden fence before we arrived.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"had measured"},{"id":"B","text":"have measuring"},{"id":"C","text":"have measured"},{"id":"D","text":"has measured"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Build **modal + have + past participle**.","explanation":"The past deduction requires **must have measured**. Have stays base after must.","keywords":["past-deduction-form"],"skill":"past-deduction-form","contextKey":"past-modals-3","fingerprint":"a7be271db92e2687b39497ac31450134be27e718fa4c059db420ae73e2838c67","source":"seed","provenance"