 claim a strong deduction that it happened, contradicting the context.","D":"Will have would express a different prediction or inference, not the requested retrospective advice."}}},{"id":"0ed49485-14eb-5e0b-aeca-48ac529a846f","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"You did the task, but it was unnecessary: “You ____ have measured the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"must not"},{"id":"B","text":"did not need"},{"id":"C","text":"should"},{"id":"D","text":"need not"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The action **happened**, and the speaker says there was **no need** for it.","explanation":"**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary.","keywords":["unnecessary-completed-action"],"skill":"unnecessary-completed-action","contextKey":"past-modals-3","fingerprint":"ff1729d1de826ac0a8055ed85d5f84e27fdde0a86c64d2509c243909ee5c20e4","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The action **happened**, and the speaker says there was **no need** for it.","**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary.","Choose **need not**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Must not have does not express the stated lack of necessity in this construction.","B":"Did not need requires to before have and is not the needn’t-have pattern.","C":"Should have would recommend the action, not say it was unnecessary.","D":"**Need not have** says the completed action was unnecessary."}}},{"id":"e5a6569a-2eb1-545a-ae75-16e65b1da735","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"Infer an ongoing past activity: “At that time, they might have ____ the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"being measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"be measuring"},{"id":"C","text":"measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"been measuring"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Combine past possibility with continuous aspect: **might have been + -ing**.","explanation":"After might have, use **been measuring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time.","keywords":["past-continuous-deduction"],"skill":"past-continuous-deduction","contextKey":"past-modals-3","fingerprint":"ed07fc15638784ba9a9bfbe00e387d3db57ffc10c2b2d8819e49710f5c885251","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Combine past possibility with continuous aspect: **might have been + -ing**.","After might have, use **been measuring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time.","Choose **been measuring**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Have requires the participle been, not being.","B":"Base be cannot follow perfect have.","C":"Been is missing between have and the -ing form.","D":"After might have, use **been measuring** to refer to an activity in progress at that past time."}}},{"id":"ebe38fd1-3dd8-5797-a359-66a2503673e5","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"Make a past deduction: “She must ____ the travel leaflet before we arrived.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"have translating"},{"id":"B","text":"have translated"},{"id":"C","text":"has translated"},{"id":"D","text":"had translated"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Build **modal + have + past participle**.","explanation":"The past deduction requires **must have translated**. Have stays base after must.","keywords":["past-deduction-form"],"skill":"past-deduction-form","contextKey":"past-modals-4","fingerprint":"9dd08aab8572aaa1c471af02286613aadfaaa0d8dc85960f01275866bee1a1ac","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Build **modal + have + past participle**.","The past deduction requires **must have translated**. Have stays base after must.","Choose **have translated**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Have needs a past participle in this simple modal-perfect construction.","B":"The past deduction requires **must have translated**. Have stays base after must.","C":"Has cannot follow a central modal.","D":"Had cannot directly follow must."}}},{"id":"bcbf671b-cfd1-5914-a8e8-a2034ca80110","topicSlug":"past-modals","level":"B2","prompt":"The task was not done, but doing it was advisable: “You ____ have translated the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"should"},{"id":"B","text":"must"},{"id":"C","text":"will"},{"id":"D","text":"can"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The clue is **advisable but not done**, pointing to should have.","explanation":"**Should have** marks the desirable action that the context says did not happen.","keywords":["past-criticism"],"skill":"past-criticism","contextKey":"past-modals-4","fingerprint":"123c3584e0f221f390a713095032f77118cbea14a5c7ad17579dc6e8695cd731","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The clue is **advisable but not done**, pointing to should have.","**Should have** marks the desirable action that the context says did not happen.","Choose **should**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Should have** marks the desirable action that the context says did not happen.","B":"Must have would claim a strong deduction that it happened, contradicting the context.","C":"Will have would express a different prediction or inference, not the requested retrospective advice.","D":"Can have does not make the norm